-- title:
--   Finite index of q^N R_w in R_w
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime, let $K_w$ be an intermediate field of the extension $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl q` which is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $R_w =$ `Rw q Kw` be the valuation subring of $K_w$ obtained by pulling back, along the structure map $K_w \to$ `PadicAlgCl q`, the valuation subring [`padicIntegers q`](def/GaloisRep_CompletionBridge.html#L20) of `PadicAlgCl q` attached to its $\mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$-valued valuation; thus $R_w$ is the ring of $w$-integers of $K_w$. Let $N$ be a natural number. The assertion is that the additive subgroup underlying the principal ideal of $R_w$ generated by the $N$-th power of the image of $q$ in $R_w$, i.e. the subgroup $q^N R_w \subseteq R_w$, has finite index: it satisfies Mathlib's `FiniteIndex` predicate. Note that only finiteness of the index is asserted, not a formula for it, and the case $N = 0$ is included (where the ideal is all of $R_w$).
--
--   This is the elementary finiteness statement that the $q$-adic filtration on the ring of integers of a finite extension $K_w/\mathbb{Q}_q$ consists of finite-index additive subgroups. It is used in the analysis of the $\mathbb{Z}$-module of invariants arising from units modulo $q$-th power levels, via [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.finrank_invariants_linHom_unitsModPow_Kw_of_basis`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.finrank_invariants_linHom_unitsModPow_Kw_of_basis).
